<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rebellion of the Barrios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Quito Revolt of 1765</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rebellion of the Barrios was an uprising of the neighbourhoods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> in 1765 against new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> taxes, especially a royal monopoly on cane liquor and stricter collection of the sales tax. Crowds drove out the authorities and the city governed itself for months before royal troops restored control in 1766.</p></div>
